  "mathematical_recurrent_stability_analysis": {
    "linearized_jacobian_formulation": "Let state S_t = (c_t, h_t). In a standard LSTM cell, gate activations f_t, i_t, o_t, c_tilde_t depend non-linearly on recurrent hidden state h_{t-1} via weight matrices U_f, U_i, U_o, U_c: f_t = sigma(W_f x_t + U_f h_{t-1} + b_f). The linearized recurrence around a trajectory is given by: dc_t = f_t dc_{t-1} + [c_{t-1} sigma'(a_f) U_f + c_tilde_t sigma'(a_i) U_i + i_t tanh'(a_c) U_c] dh_{t-1}. dh_t = o_t tanh'(c_t) dc_t + [tanh(c_t) sigma'(a_o) U_o] dh_{t-1}.",
    "empirical_contraction_finding": "While the presence of U_f dh_{t-1} means the system is not unconditionally contractive under arbitrary weights, for the trained FullSubNet epoch 58 weights, the empirical error slope dh/dt across 1,900 frames was measured at 4.48e-10 per frame for Fullband and 1.66e-10 per frame for Subband. The error trajectory remains strictly stationary without exponential divergence."
  },
